  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "Serenade song of the Ionian Islands (Heptanese), above all Zakynthos, Kefalonia and Corfu, which grew from the Italian canzonetta and serenade during the centuries of Venetian rule; the related arekia of Zakynthos belong to the same harmonised song culture. A small group of men sings in Western tonal harmony, typically in parallel thirds over a bass part, accompanied by guitars and mandolins, and kantades were widely recorded on early 78-rpm discs.",
